Z||000000||hutch84fierose||09-13-2001||06:18 AM||||I have a 1984 se and I am gonna switch some things to gt parts.  I wann awith the nose, rear bumper, decklid and the ground effects I have no idea how to do any of them Im sure they are not rocket science but I was wondering if and one had some tips or secrets that would help me out.  Is it just take off bolt on type deal or is it a little more complicated?????<BR>Thanks for your help<BR>HUTCH||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fiero_24||09-13-2001||07:05 AM||||I turned an 85 Coupe into a GT fastback.  The back clip was the hardest, but the rest was easy.  Are you doing a Fastback, or a notchback?   <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sunset_1.jpg">  <P>[<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||6
Z||000002||Voytek||09-13-2001||03:59 PM||||I changed '85 4-cyl front facia, rear bumper and all ground effects to an '87 GT (just didn't do the rear clip).  Everything fits quite well and is easy to swap.  Keep in mind that the mouldings on the door were changed to rounded ones in '87 I believe (mine didn't exactly match).<P>Also, if you're installing the ground effects on the doors and fenders, you'll need to drill some holes.  I left the ones from the doors off (one piece per door).  It actually looked quite neat without that.<P>I believe the lower ground effects from a GT (single long pieces front to rear fender) are rivetted in.  You'll need to drill out the rivets.  I used screws to re-attach on my other car.  You can use rivets too.<P>It's quite easy once you get started.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tabs||09-13-2001||05:20 PM||||It's very easy I put 87 gt front bumber,back bumber and rocker panels on my 85 coupe.||||reg||1
